data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":654,"item_id":"msg_044c53cde15e7c88016acbc9a4c87087d1a2ed752323860e1f","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"## Handoff summary\n\n### Task and constraints\n\nImplement the current Workboard requirements through Requirement 022 in the assigned repository at `/home/agent/work`. The user supplied rejection feedback for commit `7cda099e436cb9afc0b3364565357f362b5bb561` and wants the issue fixed, committed, and reported with the exact commit ID and run commands.\n\nUse the existing stack and launch contract: Node.js 22.22.1, ES modules, built-in HTTP and SQLite, browser HTML/CSS/JavaScript, `npm start`, bind to `0.0.0.0`, `PORT` default 8080, `DB_PATH` persistence, and `GET /health` returns `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`. No external application dependencies. Work only in this repository; do not access PM files, other builders, or their artifacts.\n\n### Progress\n\n- Sent a commentary update: rejection appears related to list view state remaining in Archived scope when acceptance expects Active; planned to trace filter/search state and initialization.\n- Inspected repo metadata. Current working directory `/home/agent/work`.\n- `git status --porcelain` was empty at inspection.\n- `git log -1 --oneline`: `7cda099 Add directory completion summary`.\n- Tracked files: `server.js`, `public/app.js`, `public/styles.css`, `public/index.html`, `package.json`.\n- No edits have been made.\n\n### Rejection evidence\n\nAcceptance timeouts occurred while trying to restore archived projects:\n\n- Test “063 archived and empty imports preserve flags literal data and native restart sentinels” timed out locating `Restore project` for `task-022 Import restart`.\n- Test “021 archived priorities are read-only and restored unchanged” timed out locating `Restore project` for `task-022 Priority archive`.\n\nBoth page snapshots showed the home list with `Project filter` selected as `Archived`; rows visible included those projects with `Restore project` buttons, so the exact underlying issue still needs diagnosis. The snapshot was enormous due to accumulated test-created projects.\n\n### Next steps\n\n1. Read `public/app.js`, `server.js`, and relevant HTML. Trace how project filter/search state is initialized, updated on navigation/return, and persisted across project/archive/import actions. Confirm whether the failing project row is hidden because of search, filter state, stale rendering, or other logic.\n2. Inspect the route/API and DOM generation for project rows and their action handlers. Keep existing cumulative behavior intact.\n3. Make the smallest coherent fix explaining why the test expects the target archived project row to be actionable in this state.\n4. Don’t add/run tests unless asked (the general developer instruction says not to run tests unless user asks to test or verify). Still perform necessary source review and ensure final tree is committed and clean.\n5. Commit the fix, verify `git status --porcelain` is empty, and report exact commit ID plus `npm start` run command and default environment behavior.\n\n### Preferences\n\nPrioritize maintainable, simple code. Keep commentary updates concise. Final response self-contained, include file links if referencing files, exact commit ID, and run commands.","logprobs":[]}

